\meta{venue}{Neuromodulation Conference, New York City, 2026}
\meta{representing}{BCI place — place://bci}

\p{Field notes from representing \strong{BCI place} at the Neuromodulation Conference in New York City (2026). Posters and talks are sorted into the three lenses we went in with: \strong{open-source application of devices}, \strong{deep brain imaging inference}, and \strong{sense stimulation \& distinct qualia}. Each entry is a transcription of what was publicly presented; where a captured photo contained bystanders or was marked confidential, the image is withheld and only the content is recorded.}

\p{This index is the conference lane of the \strong{BCI Landscape} ([[bcf-0051]]); the "Relation to our devices" section below threads every entry back to the Device Ledger ([[bcf-devices]], \code{place://bci/devices}).}

\subtree{\title{1 — Open-source application of devices}
\taxon{remark}
\p{Applied stimulation/recording devices, ranked by how much of the stack is actually released. The Stanford loop is the real open-source flagship; the rest are device-application platforms noted with honest openness status.}
\ul{
\li{[[conf-stanford-tms-navinibs]] — closed-loop robotic TMS-EEG on \strong{NaviNIBS + EphyNIBS} (open source). Bayesian coil-pose optimization.}
\li{[[conf-soterix-uhd-tes]] — Soterix ultra-HD tES on a 10-05 montage (commercial; device-application by function).}
\li{[[conf-ccny-hc-tdcs]] — City College / Bikson: High-Capacity tDCS at 6+ mA, benchtop \& wearable-disposable.}
\li{[[conf-ccny-wde-wound]] — City College / Bikson: printed, self-powered Wearable Disposable Electrotherapy patch.}
}
}

\subtree{\title{2 — Deep brain imaging inference}
\taxon{remark}
\p{Reaching past the scalp — either by implanting into the ECoG band, or by imaging-guided targeting of deep structures no scalp montage can localize.}
\ul{
\li{[[conf-motif-dot]] — Motif DOT: implanted electrodes track \strong{0.2--200 Hz} (vs 0.2--25 Hz scalp EEG). Also appears under category 3.}
\li{[[conf-kubanek-fus-pain]] — Kubanek/Utah: fMRI-localized tFUS into subgenual + dorsal anterior cingulate. Also appears under category 3.}
}
}

\subtree{\title{3 — Sense stimulation \& distinct qualia}
\taxon{remark}
\p{Writing \em{in} — evoking or modulating a percept — and, at the sharp end, evoking \strong{distinct, separable qualia}.}
\ul{
\li{[[conf-pitt-bidirectional-bci]] — Gaunt/RNEL: bidirectional BCI, ICMS of S1 evoking distinct tactile percepts (the flagship qualia work).}
\li{[[conf-motif-dot]] — Motif DOT: "expand the dose window" by steering the field away from the scalp.}
\li{[[conf-kubanek-fus-pain]] — Kubanek: modulating pain \em{aversiveness} (an affective quale), rapid and durable.}
\li{[[conf-ccny-hc-tdcs]] — cross-ref: VASP-100 pain tolerability is the gating percept for high-dose tDCS.}
}
\p{Partially captured (not written up): a neighboring closed-loop sensorimotor poster (5 Utah arrays, somatosensory microstimulation, a Deep-Q-network force controller) was visible only at the edge of frame and is left as a lead, not a claim.}
}

